  "worked_solution": "The symbol \"$\u00ac$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\u00acP(x):\\text{It is not true that\u00a0}x\\text{\u00a0is\u00a0}\\text{not}\\text{\u00a0greater than\u00a0}7,\n$$\n\n \n\nIn other words, $x$ is greater than $7.$ Therefore, $\u00acP(x)$ means the following:\n\n$$\n\u00acP(x):x\\text{\u00a0is greater than\u00a0}7.\n$$",
